active.description:
Redesign the agent-tool contract to align with core Scrum principles (single Product Backlog as the source of truth; sprints as the time dimension; epics as the space/thematic dimension) across four categories:
(1) Enhanced tools — scrum_orient gains sprint time-progress, active epic context, and template URI discovery;
(2) New tools — scrum_find_items unifies search across sprint and backlog with keys-based direct lookup and opt-in dependency graph, scrum_get_item_detail adds human-readable { number } input;
(3) Merged/renamed tools — scrum_get_board_health replaces scrum_get_backlog as a health-only aggregate view, scrum_get_analytics merges burndown and velocity history;
(4) Removed/converted — scrum_get_sprint, scrum_get_story, scrum_get_burndown, scrum_get_history, and scrum_get_template are retired from the tool surface;

templates are served as scrum://template/{type} MCP resources. The agent session start protocol is updated to task-driven health loading, direct-lookup patterns, and sprint-risk stance tables.
